{=============================================================================
  Carnot engine driving a Carnot refrigerator
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0186
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Teaching exercise, ULiège MECA0002, repetition R4, exercise 5 (2022-2023).
  A reservoir at 200 °C and the ambient at 30 °C drive a Carnot heat engine.
  The work drives a Carnot refrigerator that holds a cold space at -30 °C.
  Every process is reversible. The model computes the engine efficiency, the
  refrigerator COP, and the ratio of the heat given up by the hot reservoir
  to the heat given up by the cold space.

  Inputs : T_ref, T_hot, T_amb
  Outputs: eta, COP, Rapport_Q
  Units  : SI - temperatures in °C, pressures in Pa, energies in J
  Source : ULiège MECA0002, S. Quoilin, 2022-2023 - see README.md
=============================================================================}

"Data. The original adds 273.15 and stores the temperatures in kelvin."
"They are kept here in °C. The Carnot ratios add 273.15 again."
T_ref = -30 [C]                         "cold space [°C]; -30[K] + 273.15 [K] in the original"
T_hot = 200 [C]                         "hot reservoir [°C]; 200[K] + 273.15 [K] in the original"
T_amb = 30 [C]                          "ambient [°C]; 30[K] + 273.15 [K] in the original"

"Engine. Ideal Carnot cycle between the hot reservoir and the ambient."
"The efficiency is the work delivered divided by the heat exchanged with"
"the hot source, and it is fixed by the two source temperatures."
T_F_eng = T_amb                         "cold source of the engine, the ambient [°C]"
T_C_eng = T_hot                         "hot source of the engine [°C]"
eta = 1.0 - (T_F_eng + 273.15)/(T_C_eng + 273.15)   "Carnot engine efficiency [-]"

"Refrigerator. Ideal Carnot cycle between the ambient and the cold space."
"The COP is the heat extracted from the cold source divided by the work"
"received. The work received equals the work delivered by the engine."
T_F_ref = T_ref                         "cold source of the refrigerator [°C]"
T_C_ref = T_amb                         "hot source of the refrigerator, the ambient [°C]"
COP = 1.0/((T_C_ref + 273.15)/(T_F_ref + 273.15) - 1.0)   "Carnot refrigerator COP [-]"

"Ratio of the heat given up by the hot reservoir to the heat given up by"
"the cold space. With Q_C_eng = W_eng/eta, Q_F_ref = W_ref*COP and"
"W_eng = W_ref, the ratio is 1/(eta*COP), as in the original."
Rapport_Q = 1/(eta*COP)                 "heat from the hot reservoir over heat from the cold space [-]"
